Commit:     brendan@thunderbird.net <brendan@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 20 17:24:04 2026 +0000

    Bug 1999489 - Stop the storage calendar from using its statements after teardown. r=mkmelin

    The calendar finalizes its SQL statements when the profile is torn down, but a
    read can still be in flight or start afterwards - registering a cached network
    calendar kicks off a metadata read that nobody waits for. Reading the JS
    `params` accessor of a finalized statement asserts in debug builds, which is the
    intermittent crash in test_storage_connection.js.

    Refuse the statement before that accessor is used, marked with a cause so that
    only this case is swallowed: a read that outlives its calendar ends quietly -
    there is no caller left to hand the failure to. The failed queries are still
    logged.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317485

